R-CM2 R-CM20 R-PD9 R-CC2 R-CC6 R-CC7 R-CC1 R-LD4 R-LD7 R-DT5 R-SO7 R-PH8 R-AD1 R-AD22 R-SL4 R-H1 R-H3 R-RP3 R-EC17 R-EV22 R-LF3 R-BL6 R-H7 R-J3 M22 M26 M1 C2 Q4 Q1-006b R-H4 R-H9 R-AD21: the command code of `add` with the fake Fx (slice 007), 6 runs on one project (`app`, with a `.git` dir, a path entry `../lib/main.roc` out of the app dir, a path entry `./inner/main.roc` in the app dir, a module `Helpers.roc` with 2 embeds (`import "../data/notes.txt"` out of the app dir, `import "inner/data.json"` in it), a module `inner/Deep.roc` with 2 embeds (`import "../../data/deep.txt"` out, `import "data.json"` in), and a platform).
The calls of one run fix the order of Install.run!: args, env, clock, cwd, the project (canonical, list_dirs, read_files), canonical of the project file and the record in projects.json (also for a run that fails later), programs and `roc version`, then the flow, then the ladder and the write.
Run 1: a new entry. The temp copy has no `.git` (M22) and the candidate header in it has the path entry as an absolute path (M26, see the lines `copy-entries` and `|` in calls.log). Run 2: an editor changes the comment of the platform line while the probes run (the hook after the 3rd probes call). The text of the entry that Talon edits is the same, so Talon applies its edit to the new text and writes it (R-CC7): both changes are in the file. Run 3: the editor changes the version in the json entry, which Talon moves (hook after the 5th probes call): exit 17, nothing is written, the editor change stays. Run 4: the member is a package (`lib/main.roc`): 2 probes (baseline and check, no build).
Slice 006b: the path entry `../lib/main.roc` is absolute in the copy, the path entry `./inner/main.roc` stays as it is (Q4, the util `Rebase`). The kind of a new name comes from the newest candidate by `published_at` (C2 of slice 007, D6): the page of the fixture lists the oldest first, so the first read of a package is the newest release (`FaSAC...` for util, `7r2t7...` for lex). That header is a start fact of the pick, so the pick does not read it again. Run 5 (M1): `--no-check --json` gives `data.check` and `data.build` `skipped`, `probes` 0, `pinned` null, and no ladder call.
Q1 of slice 006b (all `.roc` files): after `copy_tree` the ladder walks the copy (`list_dirs` of the copy, then of `inner`, one call for each level), reads the `.roc` files except the project file (one `read_files`), and writes the candidate header and each changed file in one `write_atomic` call (header first, then the files in path order). `Rebase` makes the embeds that leave the app dir absolute (`$PROJECT/data/notes.txt`) and keeps the others. The fake `probes!` shows each import line of the other `.roc` files of the copy (lines `  ~ <path>: <line>`).
Run 6 (slice 015, R-H9, R-AD21): `add local --json`, where `local` is a path entry. Nothing changes (exit 0, no probe, no write). The human line prints the value as written and names no command (`local: ../lib/main.roc is in the header`, on stderr with `--json`). The envelope has the entry in `data.kept` with the value as the `name` and an empty `version` (a proposal, TW24).
